ns that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29435c7e-2913-51cb-b1ca-bb88c5109d0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" :answer/id #uuid "de7119fd-f799-5cbe-b151-bfa1739403a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "no solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection/e0c28e3b639c79553afd356743c7f71caedd588819de414757445d061f8e8e45" :answer/id #uuid "f65836fa-88ac-5d7a-9690-5f048bfa84db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection/24c4c3435aa3ca4566f4e45cc30240e96b3bbbfd9bb34ad9a664c82d0c8d1414" :answer/id #uuid "f76f4e48-ebd3-579d-9229-3ccac8cd9767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection/533e97630c8674f05c101017a94d868c09ef85cd6c4cb4b46d0be00aa12fc911" :answer/id #uuid "6d05d526-5375-5fad-b04f-684af95ec459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{6}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" :answer/id #uuid "a7115cbf-2a8c-5a6d-a1df-c6009058ef87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aec695a4-84bb-5965-af87-a569df499ba0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115233/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-115233/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" "q-115233/selection/e0c28e3b639c79553afd356743c7f71caedd588819de414757445d061f8e8e45" "q-115233/selection/24c4c3435aa3ca4566f4e45cc30240e96b3bbbfd9bb34ad9a664c82d0c8d1414" "q-115233/selection/533e97630c8674f05c101017a94d868c09ef85cd6c4cb4b46d0be00aa12fc911" "q-115233/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115233" :question/id #uuid "3ee54207-e6ba-5f31-8fde-08e9c4938270" :question/math-academy-id "q-115233" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1<-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1 & <-5 \\\\ 2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-6 \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $\\frac{1}{3}>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nTherefore, ${(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}$ cannot be less than $-3.$ Hence, the inequality\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}<-3\n$$\n\nhas no solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a114450f-bfcd-5db3-9060-fcd067c606fa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "960d47f8-01d6-58e9-b271-4c3534a0c237" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2c5b0654-2f1c-5c56-8b77-615143ac5f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53dfce40-243d-54b5-972d-90d655ef4d3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277887/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer-field/choices ["q-277887/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" "q-277887/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "95d8b922-5e36-5aa7-954e-179c9f926e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "07f53230-a5e4-570f-b796-40bf2a8d54be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277887/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-277887/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "93aebea1-8de4-5ef3-8d34-7b60b72c9583" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2399b3cc-e427-5f6a-a14e-906d9d78fd44" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277887/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-277887/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277887" :question/id #uuid "94b9c62a-0811-5dce-a2b5-16a90ad4772b" :question/math-academy-id "q-277887" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-(0.75)^{2-3x}<(0.98)^{3x-1}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $(0.98)^{3x-1}$ is always positive and $-(0.75)^{2-3x}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-(0.75)^{2-3x}<(0.98)^{3x-1}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-\\infty <x<\\infty \n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277887/field-1" "q-277887/field-2" "q-277887/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29435c7e-2913-51cb-b1ca-bb88c5109d0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277887"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection/0463aea4121e3ab91ccb4fa629077d1ca30980ace3c15e8b5cad518dfd883bd2" :answer/id #uuid "cae78912-b81d-555d-8d98-6f257b499c47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection/74a6cf88534f9b027a1fa78f2b9441b10a409dddb03e8cd79e9a13bbaa8f9053" :answer/id #uuid "f958928b-8f25-5bd0-b4cb-5892c64e7e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection/973e2ba21c0079638823212df1cf2519991edf6786897efbeb409e55c69e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "a78770ef-3fe3-56f7-9c05-e4d09d459051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection/46bfc87c778c43aa74df625fc6377b3ddb1c3208df84bde13d2838b99ea5a93c" :answer/id #uuid "7c68af60-ec46-574b-82f2-e0664a4d68b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection/c92ff29e28763cbde33b7fe730a7976608447a61385de828628408f389c52fbe" :answer/id #uuid "cc07a8a9-56ee-5707-a5b9-146513dfeeaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d60c77db-f966-5c7a-93a6-10618646dc03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365299/selection/973e2ba21c0079638823212df1cf2519991edf6786897efbeb409e55c69e3da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-365299/selection/0463aea4121e3ab91ccb4fa629077d1ca30980ace3c15e8b5cad518dfd883bd2" "q-365299/selection/74a6cf88534f9b027a1fa78f2b9441b10a409dddb03e8cd79e9a13bbaa8f9053" "q-365299/selection/973e2ba21c0079638823212df1cf2519991edf6786897efbeb409e55c69e3da9" "q-365299/selection/46bfc87c778c43aa74df625fc6377b3ddb1c3208df84bde13d2838b99ea5a93c" "q-365299/selection/c92ff29e28763cbde33b7fe730a7976608447a61385de828628408f389c52fbe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365299" :question/id #uuid "b94169f1-377c-5964-ba3c-f879e9c9f359" :question/math-academy-id "q-365299" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x}\\le 3\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 9\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{5}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-365299/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05f94d64-fdf7-55d8-80fb-3988a47ed2d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365299"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
